Hi Perry,

Thanks for your quick response. I added the install_github() line to the script so hopefully that should work now.

Yes, the error is surrounded by 'not all errors are a problem' sentence. The full error is:

Defining model
Building model
Setting data and initial values
Running calculate on model
  [Note] Any error reports that follow may simply reflect missing values in model variables.

Error in chol.default(model$cov_matrix[getNodeFunctionIndexedInfo(INDEXEDNODEINFO_,  :
  the leading minor of order 1 is not positive definite

Checking model sizes and dimensions
  [Note] This model is not fully initialized. This is not an error.
         To see which variables are not initialized, use model$initializeInfo().
         For more information on model initialization, see help(modelInitialization).
> model$mu
            [,1]       [,2]
 [1,]  0.3446361  0.7426614
 [2,]  0.1320599  0.3182296
...
> model$var
 [1] NA NA NA NA NA NA NA NA NA NA

The initial values of nu and tau are 1 and 0.5, respectively. In this example dt is always 0.1, but this won't always be the case as it will vary within a sample in later work.

Thanks again, and hopefully the code runs this time.

Best,
Mark

